{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>After the doings of the land of Egypt.</b> This teaches that the practices of the Egyptians and the Canaanites are the most corrupt of all the nations — and that very place where Israel dwelt was the most corrupt of all." "<b>That I bring you there.</b> This teaches that those nations who conquered Israel are the most corrupt of all (ibid.)." "<b>And in their statutes you shall not walk.</b> What did Scripture leave unsaid? Rather, these are their customs — matters decreed upon them — such as theaters and stadiums. Rabbi Meir says: these are the ways of the Amorite that the Sages enumerated (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:55.489628310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}